                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "I see the vision with this game - watching people live out their lives, gathering clues about their stories and surroundings, and having the opportunity to play god and mess with their lives as you see fit - but I feel like the execution leaves a lot to be desired. Like other reviewers have said, the constant management of hunger, money, etc feels like a drag and takes away from the appeal of the game which is watching the cages. The cages are also a bit lacking in how half of them are basically duds with no interactable elements, and the ones that are interactable are pretty repetitive and mostly just replay the same 2-3 scenes. I played one almost complete run (I couldn't quite make the final day evaluation, so the game abruptly ended) and then got about halfway through another run before I got too bored to continue. There just isn't enough variation to make it interesting, especially with the hassle of the resource management side of things. Definitely not worth the $15 price tag.",
